## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a full CAPA program around a nuanced data-leak due to a race in schema evolution, ensuring cross-tenant and cross-region considerations are baked in.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence, tenant/stream IDs, redaction configs, logs, RCA link
- Region-aware lifecycle: detect, contain, remediate, verify, close
- Minimal REST API for CAPA creation/update with linked artifacts
- Cross-tenant/region metrics: recurrence, MTTR, false positives; canary rollout
- RCA template and validation workflow

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example CAPA data model (TypeScript)
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  tenantId: string;
  streamId: string;
  evidenceUri: string;
  redactionConfigId: string;
  status: 'detected'|'contained'|'remediated'|'verified'|'closed';
  region: string;
  createdAt: string;
  linkedLogs?: string[];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you integrate with existing incident management and alerting tooling?
- How would you design canary validation across regions to prevent regression?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end CAPA design for a real multi-tenant data routing bug with data residency risk, ensuring traceability from detection to verification and rollback.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence, tenant IDs, and route metadata
- Region-aware lifecycle state machine with clear escalations
- Linked logs/traces in CAPA records for auditability
- Canary rollout and RCA templates with measurable metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal REST API skeleton for CAPA creation
app.post('/capa', (req, res) => {
  const { evidence, tenantId, routeInfo } = req.body;
  // persist CAPA and link logs/traces
  res.status(201).send({ id: 'capa-123', status: 'open' });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify false positives and tune thresholds across regions?
- What automated checks would prevent reintroduction of the misrouting in future deployments?

